Description:
    Generates authentication into your app. Only the features you pick are
    generated, and the code is yours to change.

    Pick at least one identifier (--email, --phone or --username) and one
    sign-in method (--password, --magic-link, --sms-code, --passkey or
    --omniauth).

    Not sure which flags you want? The wizard will ask you:

        bin/rails generate authnz_eleven:wizard

    Settings live in config/initializers/authentication.rb.

Examples:
    bin/rails generate authnz_eleven --email --password

    Passwordless:
        bin/rails generate authnz_eleven --email --magic-link --passkey

    GitHub-style:
        bin/rails generate authnz_eleven --username --email --password \
          --recoverable --passkey --second-factor=totp,webauthn --sudoable

    A second, separate identity:
        bin/rails generate authnz_eleven --user-class=Realtor --namespaced --email --password
